 \;">          &#160\;        </p><p style="text-align: center\;"><em><str
 ong>A Stitch in Time: Home Sewing of the 1960s and 1970s.</strong></em></
 p><p>          Take a look back in time to the home-sewn fashions of the 
 1960s and 1970s in the exhibit <em>A Stitch in Time: Home Sewing of the 1
 960s and 1970s</em>. The garments on view are from IU's own Elizabeth Sag
 e Historic Costume collection\, known for their Glenn Close Costume Colle
 ction\, haute couture\, and Hoosier native designers like Bill Blass\, Ha
 lston\, and Norman Norell.        </p><p style="text-align: center\;"><em
 >This exhibit is curated by Beth Battles for her capstone project for her
  Curatorship MA program.</em></p><p style="text-align: center\;"><em><str
