 r><td colspan="2"><p style="text-align: center\;">          &#160\;      
   </p><p style="text-align: center\;"><em><strong>The Ethics of Curation:
  Student-Curated Mulitmedia Exhibition</strong></em></p><p style="text-al
 ign: center\;">          This collaborative student-curated exhibit exami
 nes curation and its ethical dimensions. The exhibit reflects upon and re
 members the past while working to make museums and curation more inclusiv
 e in the future. Objects featured include paintings\, photography\, and d
 ioramas. Students curated this exhibit as part of the class SP26-A344 Cur
 atorial Ethics taught by Dr. Faye R. Gleisser.        </p><p style="text-
 align: center\;"><strong>Dates: April 24\, 2026-July 20\, 2026</strong></
 p><p style="text-align: center\;"><picture class="lw_image lw_image30975 
