BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Eskenazi School of Art, Architecture + Design
DTSTART:20260813T170000Z
DTEND:20260813T190000Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Homeschool Day: Ancient Money Makers
DESCRIPTION:Though small in size\, these coins are full of bold images an
 d meaning. Join us to explore ancient coins and design your own creative 
 currency inspired by history!  Program designed by our licensed art educa
 tor for students in grades K-12.Know Before You Go:  Meet us in the Simps
 on Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the museum at 1 pm. Together\
 , we'll drop off personal items before exploring the galleries. After see
 ing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll head back to the Roehm
  Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpieces! Don't forget to
  dress for a mess!  Strollers are welcome. Chaperone required. We ask tha
 t chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for every 6 children.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Though small in size\, these coins are 
 full of bold images and meaning. Join us to explore ancient coins and des
 ign your own creative currency inspired by history!</p><p>  Program desig
 ned by our licensed art educator for students in grades K-12.</p><p><stro
 ng>Know Before You Go:</strong></p><p>  Meet us in the Simpson Center for
  Education on the 2nd floor of the museum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop 
 off personal items before exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks 
 that will inspire our project\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-M
 aking Studio to create our own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a 
 mess!</p><p>  Strollers are welcome. <strong>Chaperone required.</strong>
  We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for every 6 child
 ren.</p>
UID:20260813T170000Z-2352807@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260716T121517Z
