LOCATION:Maxwell Hall\, 750 E. Kirkwood Avenue\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
GEO:39.16705;-86.524718
SUMMARY:Rural Placemaking Studio Public Design Open House
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, students from the IU Eskenazi School of Art\, A
 rchitecture + Design (https://eskenazi.indiana.edu/index.html) are workin
 g alongside community partners across rural Indiana through the Rural Pla
 cemaking Studio (https://rural.indiana.edu/focus/arts-culture/rural-place
 making-studio/index.html).  Meet the students and community partners behi
 nd the work\, and discover how these projects are helping shape vibrant r
 ural communities across Indiana.This event is free and open to the public
 . Please register to attend.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This summer\, students from the <a href
 ="https://eskenazi.indiana.edu/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 >IU Eskenazi School of Art\, Architecture + Design</a> are working alongs
 ide community partners across rural Indiana through the <a href="https://
 rural.indiana.edu/focus/arts-culture/rural-placemaking-studio/index.html"
  target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rural Placemaking Studio</a>.</p><p>  Mee
 t the students and community partners behind the work\, and discover how 
 these projects are helping shape vibrant rural communities across Indiana
 .</p><p><em>This event is free and open to the public. Please register to
  attend.</em></p>
