SUMMARY:Homeschool Day: Tabletop Treasures (AM Session)
DESCRIPTION:Students will look closely at still life paintings in the gal
 leries\, discovering how artists use symbolism and lighting to communicat
 e mood and reveal more than meets the eye. After finding inspiration in t
 he galleries\, students will create their own still life paintings by arr
 anging and observing objects at their table to tell their own unique stor
 ies!  Program designed by our licensed art educator for students in grade
 s K-12.Know Before You Go:  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education o
 n the 2nd floor of the museum at 10 am. Together\, we'll drop off persona
 l items before exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks that will i
 nspire our project\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studi
 o to create our own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!  Stro
 llers are welcome. Chaperone required. We ask that chaperones be 18 or ol
 der\, with one adult for every 6 children.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Students will look closely at still lif
 e paintings in the galleries\, discovering how artists use symbolism and 
 lighting to communicate mood and reveal more than meets the eye. After fi
 nding inspiration in the galleries\, students will create their own still
  life paintings by arranging and observing objects at their table to tell
  their own unique stories!</p><p>  Program designed by our licensed art e
 ducator for students in grades K-12.</p><p><strong>Know Before You Go:</s
 trong></p><p>  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd flo
 or of the museum at 10 am. Together\, we'll drop off personal items befor
 e exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our pr
 oject\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create o
 ur own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!</p><p>  Strollers 
 are welcome. <strong>Chaperone required.</strong> We ask that chaperones 
 be 18 or older\, with one adult for every 6 children.</p>
